# Returns as other languages write them (notes/layers.md, sugar; Rust twin: welcome_forms.rs lower_bare_returns): a
# bare `return` returns ø, the phrase `return ø` the emitter compiles. (A result arrow `x(p: P) -> int := …` is the
# parser's typed head.)
rewrite return => return ø where statement

# A value definition reading a variable, or a word that reads one, is charged (P71, wiki/charged.md): the function of
# no parameters, whose bare use is its call, so `tuning = 442; A4` follows the tuning; a constant stays a value (P70)
rewrite ($h := $e) => ($h() := $e) where $h is varying and statement
